"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4866,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":103,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["ecmascript","eslint","javascript","linter","static-code-analysis"],"visibility":"public","forks":4866,"open_issues":103,"watchers":26698,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/pulls/7859","html_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/pull/7859","diff_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/pull/7859.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/pull/7859.patch","merged_at":"2017-01-06T20:22:35Z"},"body":"**What is the purpose of this pull request? (put an \"X\" next to item)**\r\n\r\n[x] Bug fix (see https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/7852)\r\n\r\n**What changes did you make? (Give an overview)**\r\n\r\nThis updates `prefer-const` to autofix destructuring assignments with the `destructuring: any` option if all of the declarations in the destructuring pattern are fixable.\r\n\r\nPreviously, destructuring assignments were only fixed when the `destructuring` option was set to `all`, or when there was exactly one variable declared in the assignment. It looks like this was due to a limitation of passing `node` as a single parameter to a `report` function -- the function couldn't determine whether the other variables declared in the destructuring assignment were also fixable, so it only performed a fix if there was exactly one declaration.\r\n\r\nThis commit updates the rule to check all variables in a destructuring assignment at once, which makes it easier to determine whether a fix should be performed. In addition, this means that the same logic can be used for destructuring and non-destructuring assignments.\r\n\r\n**Is there anything you'd like reviewers to focus on?**\r\n\r\nNothing in particular\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/7859/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/7859/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":912848502,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDkxMjg0ODUwMg==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/912848502","actor":{"login":"vitorbal","id":626038,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNjAzOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/626038?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorbal","html_url":"https://github.com/vitorbal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorbal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorbal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorbal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorbal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorbal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorbal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorbal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorbal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vitorbal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2017-01-05T16:06:23Z","label":{"name":"accepted","color":"0052cc"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":912848503,"node_id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50OTEyODQ4NTAz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/912848503","actor":{"login":"vitorbal","id":626038,"node_id